From: wainohito <wainohito@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] platform: input method text goes to the field under a popup

Applications such as Falkon open a completer popup while text is typed,
and Qt moves its focus to it, while Haiku keeps the keyboard, and the
input method, on the window below. The text composed and committed was
sent to the popup and lost, and the candidates were put at its corner.
Send it to the focus object of the window the event arrived in, place
the candidates at that object's cursor, and do not end the composition
when the focus moves to a popup or a drag window. Also take the focus
widget into account for QQuickWidget-based views such as QtWebEngine,
whose inner item does not say it accepts input methods.

A trace of the events is written to /tmp/qhaiku-im.log while
~/config/settings/qhaiku-im-debug exists.

How this was tested: on a VAIO P (x86_gcc2h) with Falkon 23.08 and
Dooble: inline conversion in the search and address fields with their
completer popups open, and in text fields of web pages.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: wainohito <wainohito@gmail.com>
---
